    kind: invariant  # 2f42
    title: "ADR-0017's implementation-status markers are stale in five places: §3a/§3c-3d/§4b claim 'no production consumer' when they have one, and §4a/§7a say 'not implemented' when the code exists and is merely unwired"  # 2f42
    status: violated  # 2f42
    priority: 2  # 2f42
    parent:  # 2f42
    tags:  # 2f42
    - taint  # 2f42
    - adr_0017  # 2f42
    - documentation  # 2f42
    isbefore: []  # 2f42
    duplicate_of: []  # 2f42
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2f42
    pr_ref:  # 2f42
    description: "ADR-0017's implementation-status markers were measured 2026-08-02 and never\nupdated. In the six days after that measurement, PRs #188, #190, #192 and #197\nshipped four of the things the markers say do not exist. The markers still say\nit, and they are the first thing a reader consults to decide what to build.\n\nALL FIVE CLAIMS VERIFIED AGAINST THE TREE 2026-08-26 (dev daafb0abb1), not\ninferred from PR history:\n\n  §3a \"SPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED ... no production consumer\"\n      FALSE. `_ddg_taint_reaches` has TWO production call sites --\n      taint.py:3589 (the confirm-only arm) and taint.py:3645 (the WI-fasub\n      sanitizer barrier arm, where since PR #214 a False DELETES a finding).\n\n  §3a subsection banner, which describes \"what propagate_taint_ddg actually\n      does today (measured 2026-08-02)\": \"It builds the forward index\n      `ddg_forward` and the tainted-variable set `tainted_at` and reads\n      neither.\"\n      FALSE, AND UNFALSIFIABLE AS WRITTEN: neither identifier occurs anywhere\n      in taint.py any more (`grep -n \"ddg_forward\\|tainted_at\"` returns\n      nothing). The banner describes a version of the function that no longer\n      exists, in the present tense, above a subsection labelled TARGET DESIGN.\n\n  §3c-3d \"mixed-coverage verdicts ... no production consumer\"\n      FALSE. The per-verdict `analysis_methods` breakdown is emitted\n      (verify_claims.py:940) and `ddg_mixed` is a live label.\n\n  §4 function summaries \"no production consumer\"\n      HALF FALSE, and the half matters. §4b (DECLARED, YAML) is live:\n      propagate_taint_ddg calls load_function_summaries() (taint.py:3363) and\n      38 terminating entries feed _use_site_terminates. §4a (INFERRED) is dead.\n      Lumping them hides exactly the distinction WI-famig turns on.\n\n  §7a \"field-sensitivity ... SPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED\"\n      WRONG FAILURE MODE. `is_field_tainted` IS implemented\n      (taint.py:2697) and correct against its ten unit tests. It has ZERO\n      production callers -- tests only.\n\nTHE DISTINCTION THIS ITEM EXISTS TO RESTORE, and the reason this is not\ncosmetic: \"not implemented\" tells the next reader to WRITE it. \"Implemented,\nno production consumer\" tells them to WIRE it. Those are different jobs with\ndifferent costs, and the marker currently gives the wrong instruction for §4a\nand §7a both.\n\nTHIS IS THE ADR'S OWN DOCUMENTED FAILURE MODE, RECURRING. §3a already carries\na correction reading: \"`_sink_module_compatible` ... was added 2026-05-14 and\nNEVER HAD A PRODUCTION CALLER -- its only reachability was six unit tests,\nWHICH IS WHAT HELD IT AT 100% COVERAGE AND HID IT.\" `is_field_tainted` and\n`infer_summary` are that same shape, and the ADR that documents the pattern is\nnow the artifact concealing two more instances of it.\n\nONE FACT, TWO HOMES, AND THE SECOND SILENTLY WON (L7). taint.py's own module\ndocstring ALREADY corrects the §4 claim in place -- \"THAT PARAGRAPH USED TO END\n'§4a and §4b have zero production callers' ... Half of it is now false and it\nwas load-bearing, so it is corrected rather than deleted\". The correction was\nwritten into the code and never propagated to the ADR, so the two artifacts\ndisagree and the one a reader reaches first is the stale one.\n\nREMEDY (docs-only, no behaviour change):\n  1. Rewrite the top-of-file Status line per-subsection, splitting §4a from §4b\n     and distinguishing \"no implementation\" from \"implemented, unwired\".\n  2. Replace the §3a banner's stale present-tense description; the walk exists\n     and is confirm-only, which is what the subsection should say.\n  3. State for §7a and §4a that the code exists and is unwired, naming the\n     symbol, so the next reader can find it.\n\nDO NOT ALSO EDIT THE ADR-0037 / ADR-0038 SUPERSESSION BANNERS. Those are a\nseparate axis and were not re-verified here; touching them would smuggle an\nunverified change into a docs correction.\n\nSCOPE CHECK PERFORMED, so the next reader need not repeat it: this is\nADR-0017 only. Whether other ADRs carry status markers measured once and\ninherited is NOT established by this item and should not be assumed from it."  # 2f42
    fields:  # 2f42
      statement: "An ADR's implementation-status marker must describe the tree as it is. A subsection labelled SPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED must have no production consumer, and a subsection whose code exists but is unreachable from production must say so in those terms — because 'not implemented' and 'implemented but unwired' instruct the reader to do different jobs at different costs."  # 2f42
      root_cause: "The markers carry a one-time measurement date (2026-08-02) and were never re-measured. PRs #188, #190, #192 and #197 landed in the six days after, each shipping something a marker denies. taint.py's docstring was corrected in place; the correction never propagated to the ADR, so the same fact has two homes and the one a reader reaches first is stale."  # 2f42
