  nonce: '5295'  # 5295
  message: "FIXED IN PR #548 (dev bd638f8cbf). Docs-only; no behaviour change.\n\nThree edits, each anchored on a whole block with an assert-count-1 single-pass\nscript so a wrong anchor aborted before any write:\n  1. Top-of-file Status line rewritten PER SUBSECTION, splitting 4a from 4b and\n     distinguishing \"no implementation\" from \"implemented, unwired\".\n  2. The section 3a banner's stale present-tense description replaced. It now\n     states that the walk RUNS and is CONFIRM-ONLY, names both production call\n     sites (taint.py:3589 confirm-only, taint.py:3645 sanitizer barrier), and\n     records the two blockers it used to name that are CLOSED (#188/#203\n     re-keying, and step 5 as argument-at-the-sink) rather than deleting them.\n  3. The Phase 3 table row split into 4b (yes) / 4a (no).\n\nI DID NOT TOUCH the ADR-0037 / ADR-0038 supersession banners, per this item's\nown instruction -- they are a separate axis and were not re-verified.\n\nTWO THINGS FOUND WHILE FIXING, both recorded rather than silently absorbed:\n\n(a) THE DOCUMENT DISAGREED WITH ITSELF, which the filing understated. The\nPhase 2 table row three hundred lines below the Status line was ACCURATE AND\nCURRENT -- it already said \"section 7a field-sensitivity: still NO production\ncaller (is_field_tainted)\" and \"section 3a propagation: confirm-only\". So this\nwas not one stale line but one fact in four homes with the stalest one on top,\nwhich is the ordering that matters because it is the one a reader reaches first.\n\n(b) A SIXTH STALE FIGURE, in taint.py rather than the ADR. Its module docstring\nsays the live index \"holds 38 terminating summaries ... that this walk\nconsults\". Counted live: 113 index entries, 76 terminating, 55 of them bare\naliases the walk never consults (it uses qualified names only), so the figure\nthe sentence means is 41. I did NOT propagate 38 into the ADR and I did not pin\n41 either -- the same docstring argues three paragraphs later that a hardcoded\ncount is \"a rationale that decays with nobody deciding anything\" because the\nalias index moved 33 -> 108 -> 113 in two days. The ADR text now states the\nproperty without a number. The stale 38 in taint.py is left in place: it is a\nsource edit, not a docs edit, and this item is scoped docs-only.\n\nSCOPE UNCHANGED: this remains ADR-0017 only. Whether other ADRs carry status\nmarkers measured once and inherited is still NOT established, and should not be\ninferred from this closure."  # 5295
